From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ofono-binder: A card without applications is no error

Since 1.1.42 ("Handle SIMs with no apps") a card without applications,
like an eUICC without an enabled profile, counts as inserted. oFono then
reads its files every 20 seconds, and binder_sim_append_path() logged
"Unsupported app type 0" as an error each time, though the path falls
back to the MF as before. Only a debug message for such a card; any other
unknown application type stays an error.
---
  src/binder_sim.c | 9 +++++++++
  1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/binder_sim.c b/src/binder_sim.c
--- a/src/binder_sim.c
+++ b/src/binder_sim.c
@@ -424,6 +424,15 @@ binder_sim_append_path(
         len = ofono_get_ef_path_3g(fileid, db_path);
     } else if (app_type == RADIO_APP_TYPE_SIM) {
         len = ofono_get_ef_path_2g(fileid, db_path);
+    } else if (app_type == RADIO_APP_TYPE_UNKNOWN) {
+        /*
+         * A card without applications (an eUICC without an enabled
+         * profile) counts as inserted since 1.1.42, and oFono reads
+         * its files over and over: from the MF, below, as before.
+         * That is expected there, not an error.
+         */
+        DBG_(self, "no application, file %04x from the MF", fileid);
+        len = 0;
     } else {
         ofono_error("Unsupported app type %d", app_type);
         len = 0;
